          %title Field variations
          %h2#FieldVariations Field variations
          %p In this chapter we discuss these topics:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "##JetBundles"} Jet bundles
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#DifferentialOperators"} Differential operators
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#VariationaCalculusAndVariationalBicomplex"} Variational calculus and the Variational bicomplex
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            as in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FieldsAndFieldBundles"}
            above, then we know what
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            of quantities the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+histories"} field histories
            assign to a given spacetime point (a given
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/event"} event
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            of any spacetime point (remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JetBundleInTermsOfSyntheticDifferentialGeometry"}
            below). This means equivalently that the realized field histories should be those that satisfy a given
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivatives"} partial derivatives
            of the field history at any spacetime point. This is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} equation of motion
            of the field theory (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeEquationsOnTrivialVectorFieldBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below).
          %p
            In order to formalize this, it is useful to first collect all the possible partial derivatives that a field history may have at any given point into one big space of “field derivatives at spacetime points”. This collection is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below.
          %p
            Moving around in this space means to change the possible value of fields and their derivatives, hence to
            %em vary
            the fields. Accordingly
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            of fields is just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+calculus"} differential calculus
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VariationalBicomplexOnSecondOrderJetBundleOverTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p#JetBundles
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundles"} jet bundles
          #JetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
                over
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+fiber"} field fiber
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = \mathbb{R}^{b\vert s}
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi^a)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              a natural number, the
              %em
                order-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi J
                              %mi Σ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi jb
                                    %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    J^k_{\Sigma}( E )
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{jb_k}}
                    \\\
                    \\Sigma
                    }
            %p
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \coloneqq \Sigma \times F
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ,
                          %mi μ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mn 2
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi k
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    (x^\mu)
                    \\,,\,
                    (\phi^a )
                    \\,,\,
                    ( \phi^a_{,\mu} )
                    \\,,\,
                    ( \phi^a_{,\mu_1\mu_2} )
                    \\,,\,
                    \\cdots
                    \\,,\,
                    ( \phi^a_{,\mu_1 \cdots \mu_k} )
                    \\,,\,
