            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+dimensional+manifold"} infinite dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            on jet bundles turn out to
            %em locally
            depend on only finitely many of the jet coordinates (i.e. only on a finite order of spacetime derivatives). This is the content of the following prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JetBundleIsLocallyProManifold"}
          %p
            This reflects the
            %em locality
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            defined over
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundles"} jet bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+series"} Taylor series
            expansion of fields the function at one point over spacetime could in fact depend on field history values at a
            %em different
            point of spacetime. Such non-local dependence is ruled out by prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JetBundleIsLocallyProManifold"}
            below.
          %p In practice this means that the situation is very convenient:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Any given
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian+density"} local Lagrangian density
                (which will define a field theory, we come to this in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
                below) will locally depend on some finite number
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                of derivatives and may hence locally be treated as living on the ordinary manifold
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
